comment.body:
Heads up: while reviewing #110 we caught one more endpoint with the same `if let Some` metadata-None fall-through that #110's audit listed as safe — `handle_get_hls_content` (the GET sibling of `handle_head_hls_content`):

```rust
if let Ok(Some(ref meta)) = get_blob_metadata(&hash) { … access_for(…) … }
// falls through unconditionally
match download_hls_content(&gcs_path, None) { Ok(resp) => /* serves bytes */ … }
```

When KV metadata is `None` (post-vanish, with HLS files surviving the best-effort `delete_blob_gcs_artifacts` cleanup), access control is silently skipped and HLS variant playlists / `.ts` segments are served from GCS. The `Ok(...)` pattern is also strictly worse than the original bug because it swallows transient KV errors as "no metadata, allow" instead of failing closed.

Filed #111 as a follow-up that mirrors #110's policy (404 for non-admin, log + allow for admin) and switches to `match get_blob_metadata(&hash)?` so KV errors propagate. Leaving this issue open until both #110 and #111 land.
